  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political situation in Indonesia has intensified following reports that Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka has communicated his intention to resign to President Prabowo Subianto. This development occurs alongside ongoing parliamentary discussions regarding a potential motion for an opinion regarding his position. Various political parties, including the National Awakening Party (PKB) and NasDem, have emphasized that legislative procedures, such as the expression of opinion process, will proceed regardless of the Vice President's personal plans. Legal experts and government officials have stated that if the resignation is finalized, the President is constitutionally required to propose two candidates for the vice-presidency to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR). The situation has sparked broader discourse regarding the country's political stability and the potential impact on national investment, as the transition process remains a focal point of public and political attention.",
